# Look-around: \@= \@! \@<= \@<! and their limits.

=== \@= requires a match after without including it
ref:    pattern.txt */\@=*
quote:  foo\(bar\)\@=		"foo" in "foobar"
given:  |foobaz foobar
keys:   :s/foo\(bar\)\@=/(&)/g<CR>
expect: |foobaz (foo)bar

=== \@= followed by more pattern matches at the same position
ref:    pattern.txt */\@=*
quote:  foo\(bar\)\@=foo	nothing
given:  |foobarfoo
keys:   :s/foo\(bar\)\@=foo/X/e<CR>
expect: |foobarfoo

=== \@! requires no match after
ref:    pattern.txt */\@!*
quote:  foo\(bar\)\@!		any "foo" not followed by "bar"
given:  |foobar foobaz
keys:   :s/foo\(bar\)\@!/(&)/g<CR>
expect: |foobar (foo)baz

=== \@! after a lazy multi
ref:    pattern.txt */\@!*
quote:  a.\{-}p\@!		"a", "ap", "app", "appp", etc. not immediately followed by a "p"
given:  |appq
keys:   :s/a.\{-}p\@!/(&)/<CR>
expect: |(app)q

=== \@! after .* matches to the end of the line
ref:    pattern.txt */\@!*
quote:  "\"a.*p\\@!\" will match from an \"a\" to the end of the line, because \".*\" can match all characters in the line and the \"p\" doesn't match at the end of the line."
given:  |xapp
keys:   :s/a.*p\@!/(&)/<CR>
expect: |x(app)

=== \@! before the match does not look behind
ref:    pattern.txt */\@!*
quote:  "\"\\(foo\\)\\@!bar\" will match \"bar\" in \"foobar\", because at the position where \"bar\" matches, \"foo\" does not match."
given:  |foobar
keys:   :s/\(foo\)\@!bar/(&)/<CR>
expect: |foo(bar)

=== \@! finds foo in a line without bar
ref:    pattern.txt */\@!*
quote:  Useful example: to find "foo" in a line that does not contain "bar":
given:
  |x foo bar
  y foo
keys:   /^\%(.*bar\)\@!.*\zsfoo<CR>
expect:
  x foo bar
  y |foo

=== if not followed by then
ref:    pattern.txt */\@!*
quote:  if \(\(then\)\@!.\)*$	"if " not followed by "then"
given:
  |if a then b
  if a else b
keys:   :%s/if \(\(then\)\@!.\)*$/X/<CR>
expect:
  if a then b
  |X

=== \@<= requires a match before
ref:    pattern.txt */\@<=*
quote:  \(an\_s\+\)\@<=file	"file" after "an" and white space or an end-of-line
given:  |a file an file
keys:   :s/\(an\_s\+\)\@<=file/(&)/g<CR>
expect: |a file an (file)

=== \@<= looks back across a line break
ref:    pattern.txt */\@<=*
quote:  But to limit the time needed, only the line where what follows matches is searched, and one line before that (if there is one).
given:
  |an
  file
keys:   :%s/\(an\_s\+\)\@<=file/X/<CR>
expect:
  an
  |X

=== \@<= allows a variable-width look-behind
ref:    pattern.txt */\@<=*
quote:  Like "(?<=pattern)" in Perl, but Vim allows non-fixed-width patterns.
given:  |aab b ab
keys:   :s/\(a\+\)\@<=b/(&)/g<CR>
expect: |aa(b) b a(b)

=== \zs instead of \@<=
ref:    pattern.txt */\@<=*
quote:  \([a-z]\+\)\zs,\1		",abc" in "abc,abc"
given:  |abc,abc
keys:   :s/\([a-z]\+\)\zs,\1/(&)/<CR>
expect: |abc(,abc)

=== \@1<= only looks back one byte
ref:    pattern.txt */\@<=*
quote:  This will try matching "<" only one byte before "span", which is the only place that works anyway.
given:  |<span x span
keys:   :s/<\@1<=span/(&)/g<CR>
expect: |<(span) x span

=== \@<! requires no match before
ref:    pattern.txt */\@<!*
quote:  \(foo\)\@<!bar		any "bar" that's not in "foobar"
given:  |foobar xbar
keys:   :s/\(foo\)\@<!bar/(&)/g<CR>
expect: |foobar x(bar)

=== \@<! with .* in the look-behind
ref:    pattern.txt */\@<!*
quote:  \(\/\/.*\)\@<!in	"in" which is not after "//"
given:  |in // in
keys:   :s/\(\/\/.*\)\@<!in/(&)/g<CR>
expect: |(in) // in

=== \@<! sees the previous line
ref:    pattern.txt */\@<!*
quote:  Thus this matches if there is no position in the current or previous line where the atom matches such that it ends just before what follows.
given:
  |a
  b
  b
keys:   :%s/\(a\n\)\@<!b/X/<CR>
expect:
  a
  b
  |X
